  "description": "Sr₃NaSbO₆ crystallizes in the trigonal R̅3c space group. Na is bonded in a 6-coordinate geometry to six equivalent O atoms. All Na-O bond lengths are 2.43 Å. Sr is bonded in a 8-coordinate geometry to eight equivalent O atoms. There are a spread of Sr-O bond distances ranging from 2.54-2.95 Å. Sb is bonded in an octahedral geometry to six equivalent O atoms. All Sb-O bond lengths are 2.04 Å. O is bonded to one Na, four equivalent Sr, and one Sb atom to form a mixture of distorted corner, edge, and face-sharing ONaSr₄Sb octahedra. The corner-sharing octahedral tilt angles range from 0-63°.",
